<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Auxilia</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as auxiliary troops</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The auxilia were the non-citizen troops of the Roman imperial army, recruited from provincial peoples. They provided infantry, cavalry and specialist units such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/archery">archers</a>, serving alongside the citizen legions. After long service they received Roman citizenship, which helped integrate provincials into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/auxilia.jpg" alt="Auxilia" width="320" height="221" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CristianChirita · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Engineering_corps_traian_s_column_river_crossing.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
